Subject: [PATCH 12/12] Fix: a zero refresh rate sleeps the emu thread for 35 minutes

NativeFrame ends with a fallback throttle for the menu:

    float refreshRate = System_GetPropertyFloat(SYSPROP_DISPLAY_REFRESH_RATE);
    static double lastTime = 0.0;
    if (lastTime > 0.0) {
        int sleepTimeUs = (int)(1000000 * ((1.0 / refreshRate) - diffTime));
        if (sleepTimeUs > 0)
            sleep_us(sleepTimeUs, "fallback-throttle");
    }
    lastTime = time_now_d();

On SDL, refreshRate is g_RefreshRate, taken verbatim from
displayMode->refresh_rate. SDL documents that as 0 when it cannot determine one,
and 0 is what the Emscripten video driver reports — a browser cannot be asked
what the monitor is doing.

So 1.0 / refreshRate is +inf, and (int)(1000000 * inf) saturates to INT_MAX
under wasm's non-trapping float-to-int. That is 2147483647 microseconds: a
35-minute sleep on the emu thread, inside a frame it never returns from.

`static double lastTime = 0.0` is why this presents as *exactly two frames*. The
first frame takes the lastTime > 0.0 branch as false and only records the time;
the second computes the sleep and never comes back. Measured, not inferred: with
the traces from patches 0010 and 0011 on, a run shows two complete NativeFrame
passes and two complete render handshakes — both frames submitted, presented and
fenced — and then no third frame, with the emu thread alive and silent for the
rest of the run.

Two hunks, because the bug has a source and a blast radius and both are worth
closing:

- SDLMain keeps its own 60 Hz default when SDL reports no rate, rather than
  overwriting it with zero. This is where the wrong value enters.
- NativeApp defends the division. Any platform that reports 0 — or NaN, which
  the !(x > 0) form also catches — can otherwise stop the emu thread dead, and a
  35-minute sleep is too spectacular a failure to leave one caller away.

Neither hunk is WebAssembly-specific. This is an upstream bug that needed a
platform with no queryable refresh rate to show itself.

diff --git a/SDL/SDLMain.cpp b/SDL/SDLMain.cpp
index 1bb399fd9..a15c732fd 100644
--- a/SDL/SDLMain.cpp
+++ b/SDL/SDLMain.cpp
@@ -1833,7 +1833,16 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[]) {
 	}
 	g_DesktopWidth = displayMode->w;
 	g_DesktopHeight = displayMode->h;
-	g_RefreshRate = displayMode->refresh_rate;
+	// SDL documents refresh_rate as 0 when it cannot determine one, and that is the
+	// normal answer from the Emscripten video driver: a browser cannot be asked what the
+	// monitor is doing. Keeping the 60 Hz default above is the right answer; overwriting
+	// it with zero is catastrophic two files away, because NativeFrame's fallback
+	// throttle divides by it.
+	if (displayMode->refresh_rate > 0.0f) {
+		g_RefreshRate = displayMode->refresh_rate;
+	} else {
+		WARN_LOG(Log::System, "Display reports no refresh rate; keeping %0.1f Hz", g_RefreshRate);
+	}
 	SDL_free(displayIDs);
 
 	// TODO: Should only call this if we actually intend to use OpenGL.
